Read `.claude/CLAUDE.md` in the repository root. It is the canonical project
context; `AGENTS.md`, `.opencode/AGENTS.md`, and `.gemini/GEMINI.md` are all
symlinks to it. Edit that file, never a copy.

Load-bearing points, so they apply even before that file is read:

- **Status: planning. No implementation code exists.** Anything resembling a
  build is new work, not maintenance.
- **Exactly one LLM call in the whole system** — drafting a session log at
  session end. Never on the read path, never on a background timer.
- **Append, never reconcile.** No gardening pass, no dedupe-on-write, no
  background contradiction detection.
- **Capture is automatic; sharing is manual.** A hook drafts locally; `publish`
  is the only path into shared memory, and it strips private blocks and runs a
  secret scan first.
- **`docs/` and `_drafts/` are gitignored on purpose.** `docs/` is internal
  strategy; `_drafts/` is the privacy boundary made structural. Never un-ignore
  either.
- **No business logic in command handlers.** Commands parse arguments, call an
  operation, render a result.
- Do not commit or push unless asked.
